      "message": "Hi Abe,\n\nThanks for the patch.\n\n\u003e  Once the kernel was ready at ToT, we\u0027d flip the EC config to enable the host command.\n\nTo clarify, we\u0027d be sending the EC command from the user space directly (mode entry via sysfs is still WIP upstream, especially when one includes USB4 which is an almost-alt-mode). That said this approach sounds good.\n\n\u003e I can see some downsides to this\n\nCould you elaborate on what these are? (I\u0027m not familiar with EC branch management so will put this question down to my ignorance :) )",
